Inspect the existing `claude-animated-shorts` skill and replace its ElevenLabs text-to-speech dependency with locally hosted Chatterbox TTS.

Requirements:

1. Read `SKILL.md`, all relevant audio scripts, configuration files, and the existing ElevenLabs integration before changing anything.
2. Identify every ElevenLabs dependency used for narration. Distinguish narration from music and sound effects; do not break existing audio assets or unrelated integrations.
3. Implement a local Chatterbox TTS adapter that accepts narration text and writes audio to the exact path and format expected by the existing pipeline.
4. Prefer running Chatterbox as a persistent local HTTP service rather than loading the model for every line. Keep model inference isolated in its own Python environment.
5. Preserve the current scene generation, shot planning, Remotion rendering, audio mixing, ducking, loudness normalization, and final export workflow.
6. Add configuration for the TTS backend (`chatterbox` or `elevenlabs`) so I can switch providers without editing source code.
7. Handle long narration, audio duration, sample rate, stereo/mono conversion, errors, timeouts, and missing model dependencies safely. Do not silently produce empty audio files.
8. Add a smoke test that generates a short narration, validates the output file, and confirms that the existing render pipeline can consume it.
9. Keep changes minimal and document installation, model download, startup, configuration, and troubleshooting.
10. Never print, commit, overwrite, or expose my ElevenLabs API key. Do not remove the existing ElevenLabs implementation until the Chatterbox path has passed its tests.

First report the current audio pipeline and the files you intend to change. Then implement the smallest working change, run available tests, and report the exact commands needed to generate a short.

Use the official Chatterbox implementation: https://github.com/resemble-ai/chatterbox. Do not invent Python APIs; verify the installed version's interface.
